[8307]={["atomIDs"]={"8307:description:1-67","8307:description:70-189","8307:description:192-253","8307:description:258-343","8307:description:346-423","8307:description:426-507","8307:objective:1-101"},["editorialVersion"]=2,["endingAtomIDs"]={"8307:completion:1-65","8307:completion:67-156"},["opening"]="Calandrath struggles with the desert's restricted ingredients and bitter sandworm meat. Twilight hunters seem to make a meal of it, so their camp may hold a recipe worth learning.",["pending"]="{actor} would investigate the Twilight camp's cooking information.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} found a recipe among common and unusual dishes that used sandworm meat.",["sourceHash"]="41f56d2b26a0f9252a6a97fb969b04ba8bab0ddd0beacad24b2bedd74fedfe5e",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8308]={["aftermath"]="Rutgar urged keeping watch for Brann should entry to the city become possible.",["atomIDs"]={"8308:description:1-23","8308:description:28-86","8308:description:88-104","8308:description:106-137","8308:description:142-173","8308:description:175-214","8308:description:216-240","8308:description:242-283","8308:description:285-294","8308:description:299-330","8308:description:332-393","8308:description:398-433","8308:description:443-492","8308:objective:1-81"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8308:completion:1-25","8308:completion:27-95","8308:completion:97-150"},["opening"]="Brann's letter reported deaths, an ancient battle and a tunnel toward the sealed city. His warning of a cultist and concern for his monkey accompanied uncertainty about his own survival.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to take the letter to Brann's camp.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered it to Rutgar.",["sourceHash"]="f22c4ea571e6b4ea29a3aa19f18eec142449b733afdace3aa6f273af1c13630a",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8309]={["aftermath"]="Rutgar could not read them and hoped Frankal's separate research would help.",["atomIDs"]={"8309:description:1-126","8309:description:128-212","8309:description:217-271","8309:description:273-349","8309:description:354-406","8309:description:408-465","8309:objective:1-188","8309:objective:193-283","8309:objective:285-341"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8309:completion:1-44","8309:completion:46-78","8309:completion:80-138"},["opening"]="Increased hive activity after the expedition might be linked to glyph-covered crystals. Rutgar supplied tools to copy all three sites before attempting an explanation.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to make rubbings in each hive.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the three sets of glyphs.",["sourceHash"]="059d1d9b00da34b39f945f8fc95475c1aea60fda7e9f45469e1bd25259e97de5",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8310]={["atomIDs"]={"8310:description:1-129","8310:description:131-145","8310:description:147-161","8310:description:163-176","8310:description:178-251","8310:description:253-310","8310:objective:1-167","8310:objective:169-220"},["opening"]="Frankal proposed an elixir to make the insects' language more understandable. A brain from each hive's type was the experiment he hoped would give Rutgar's work meaning.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather the three kinds of brain.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Frankal with the specimens.",["sourceHash"]="961aee7bf73e872b0604f62951d24219a8f587754c8d04233e48b276d71cadfc",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8311]={["atomIDs"]={"8311:description:1-61","8311:description:64-137","8311:description:140-222","8311:description:227-351","8311:description:354-430","8311:description:433-488","8311:objective:1-109","8311:objective:112-184","8311:objective:189-316"},["editorialVersion"]=2,["endingAtomIDs"]={"8311:completion:1-22","8311:completion:25-39","8311:completion:44-82","8311:completion:85-149","8311:completion:154-176"},["opening"]="Illness keeps Jesper from Hallow's End's usual round of tricks and sweets. A substitute can visit the three Alliance capitals and Talvash, then exchange their treats with him at the orphanage.",["pending"]="{actor} would bring Jesper the four requested city sweets.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned with the treats, delighting Jesper with the completed round.",["sourceHash"]="b8273c85a7fe3d766b1eca6c39ed1c88ba6e59d449ed1ecc826d241ab707210d",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8312]={["atomIDs"]={"8312:description:1-61","8312:description:64-137","8312:description:140-222","8312:description:227-351","8312:description:354-432","8312:description:435-490","8312:objective:1-111","8312:objective:114-186","8312:objective:191-321"},["editorialVersion"]=2,["endingAtomIDs"]={"8312:completion:1-22","8312:completion:25-39","8312:completion:44-82","8312:completion:85-149","8312:completion:154-176"},["opening"]="Spoops wants to trade for the candy a healthy child could gather in person. The Horde's three city innkeepers and Kali Remik each offer a treat for a suitable trick.",["pending"]="{actor} would bring Spoops the four requested sweets.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the completed collection to Spoops at the orphanage.",["sourceHash"]="b2c04e03367ac8ef4a8da1b90bdd6cc49adebeb776dbc52410ac8dd8ff3a10cb",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8313]={["atomIDs"]={"8313:description:1-120","8313:description:123-219","8313:objective:1-69"},["editorialVersion"]=2,["endingAtomIDs"]={"8313:completion:1-28","8313:completion:33-57","8313:completion:60-150","8313:completion:153-174"},["opening"]="The sandworm recipe uses unfamiliar names for its herbs. Calandrath's knowledge of desert plants may turn a legible but puzzling page into something useful.",["pending"]="{actor} would bring Calandrath the Torn Recipe Page.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the page; Calandrath recognized the herbs and offered instruction.",["sourceHash"]="8968534f4c6e6ffedc1bd4e4e06ff42b0115fa7b5bf28f5d10c88fda9ce46f29",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8314]={["aftermath"]="She explained that shifting layers required alignment, leaving a grim surface clue as the next lead.",["atomIDs"]={"8314:description:1-41","8314:description:43-134","8314:description:136-253","8314:description:258-315","8314:description:317-388","8314:description:393-463","8314:description:466-491","8314:objective:1-150"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8314:completion:1-93","8314:completion:95-229","8314:completion:231-239","8314:completion:244-321","8314:completion:323-444"},["opening"]="The rubbings could be reproduced, but their messages remained locked. Rutgar sent the prism to Larksbane after recognizing a communications system rather than learning its actual content.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring the prism to the Hold.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered it to Larksbane.",["sourceHash"]="50aa8a056d7ca26cfbee67922544e47ee18c99b531918bba9f7776fa2586fa6b",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8315]={["aftermath"]="Larksbane welcomed what she described as twenty thousand years of history in her hands.",["atomIDs"]={"8315:description:1-107","8315:description:109-177","8315:description:179-241","8315:description:246-341","8315:description:343-430","8315:description:432-474","8315:description:476-510","8315:objective:1-127","8315:objective:132-264","8315:objective:266-352","8315:objective:354-398","8315:objective:403-437"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8315:completion:1-47"},["opening"]="Larksbane interpreted the image as a meeting and possible summons at dragon bones. Recreating its code in sand might draw an emissary carrying the mechanism that could unlock the crystals.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to summon the emissary and recover its mechanism.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the unlocking mechanism.",["sourceHash"]="6415780e023d12b26ff6836d97f73f59439bf1e79b3e07cf9cd2fcedcac3abee",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8317]={["atomIDs"]={"8317:description:1-36","8317:description:39-120","8317:description:123-187","8317:objective:1-72"},["editorialVersion"]=2,["endingAtomIDs"]={"8317:completion:1-10","8317:completion:12-31","8317:completion:33-76","8317:completion:78-141"},["opening"]="With the recipe understood, Calandrath wants dumplings ready for the day. Help preparing a batch can put the Twilight camp's unlikely culinary knowledge to local use.",["pending"]="{actor} would bring Calandrath ten Smoked Desert Dumplings.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied the dumplings that Calandrath found unexpectedly good.",["sourceHash"]="a00922ab05aa938a0a7379405de47310669d81cb512d8164ced44b49fe0a7631",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8318]={["aftermath"]="Bor stored them in case they became useful later.",["atomIDs"]={"8318:description:1-97","8318:description:100-142","8318:description:147-216","8318:description:219-283","8318:description:286-358","8318:objective:1-67"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8318:completion:1-10","8318:completion:13-65"},["opening"]="Bor did not need to read the cult's small papers to see their use. Removing the encoded communications from circulation could hinder coordination while preserving possible information for later study.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather ten encrypted texts.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the papers to Bor.",["sourceHash"]="245f1d9720151caaec048179bd11f2a961a579b096760edb757873b485df5e16",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8320]={["aftermath"]="Huum hoped their loss would slow the cult's plans.",["atomIDs"]={"8320:description:1-118","8320:description:121-245","8320:description:250-342","8320:description:345-405","8320:description:408-474","8320:objective:1-73"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8320:completion:1-35","8320:completion:38-119","8320:completion:122-158"},["opening"]="Huum suspected a connection between cult rituals and the desert's red crystals but lacked the plan behind them. He chose the local geolords as an immediate leadership target while the larger mystery remained.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to confront ten geolords.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Huum's camp assignment.",["sourceHash"]="ccfeeca7c034c1c24049c796f9801e5924a4696239228c54b9ff3de2d2d42ad0",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8321]={["aftermath"]="Huum confirmed Vyral's death and judged the blow difficult for the remaining cultists to repair.",["atomIDs"]={"8321:description:1-72","8321:description:75-159","8321:description:162-260","8321:description:263-312","8321:description:317-335","8321:description:338-389","8321:objective:1-60"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8321:completion:1-15","8321:completion:18-33","8321:completion:36-108","8321:completion:110-240"},["opening"]="A newly discovered northeastern cave held the cult's local leader. Vyral's signet would provide evidence that the campaign had reached beyond the scattered camps.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover Vyral's signet.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the ring to Huum.",["sourceHash"]="710b7160481aa7c95448902e0137cb0aaa6e33c62792bf5f113f842a910fd419",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8322]={["atomIDs"]={"8322:description:1-101","8322:description:104-237","8322:description:242-326","8322:description:329-401","8322:description:406-501","8322:objective:1-77"},["editorialVersion"]=2,["endingAtomIDs"]={"8322:completion:1-27","8322:completion:32-121","8322:completion:123-171"},["opening"]="Yanka turns Hallow's End toward a prank against Southshore's prized ale. Rotten eggs in the inn's main keg will spoil its contents, but the intruder should expect resistance.",["pending"]="{actor} would place the eggs in the Southshore keg.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} placed the rotten eggs in the brew keg.",["sourceHash"]="19b77c5812fea200422001bcc1064ac3cc98852a5a675e49c61c8b112acb0964",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8323]={["aftermath"]="Ortell promised decoding and a way to send back anything of interest.",["atomIDs"]={"8323:description:1-101","8323:description:106-192","8323:description:197-315","8323:description:320-441","8323:description:444-508","8323:objective:1-64"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8323:completion:1-10","8323:completion:13-61","8323:completion:64-143"},["opening"]="With the lexicon available, Ortell could read his former sect's monthly bulletin. He wanted news of the hunt for him and offered to share other useful discoveries from its encoded texts.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to collect ten texts for Ortell.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought him the papers.",["sourceHash"]="df71d92135976d017d4df9875a11cb49aa29136722277590bc9125ddfaa7fb75",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8331]={["atomIDs"]={"8331:description:1-88","8331:description:90-120","8331:description:123-312","8331:description:315-372","8331:description:377-457","8331:description:460-505","8331:objective:1-43"},["opening"]="Earlier hopes of slowing the cult proved mistaken. Huum's new evidence pointed to a darker council directing it through wind stones, requiring Aurel's craft before an attack on that power.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to consult Aurel about the council.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met the craftswoman.",["sourceHash"]="6151376d2a43b669014585a05198374d97d6039fe85f65c25790c75c2ec909cb",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8332]={["aftermath"]="Aurel completed the medallion and explained that it had to be worn with the cult's other trappings.",["atomIDs"]={"8332:description:1-84","8332:description:87-229","8332:description:236-303","8332:description:306-413","8332:description:418-458","8332:objective:1-86"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8332:completion:1-14","8332:completion:16-122","8332:completion:127-139","8332:completion:141-166","8332:completion:171-256","8332:completion:258-389"},["opening"]="An ambush through a wind stone required the council to mistake an intruder for a middle-ranking cult leader. Aurel could forge the necessary medallion from a shard and templar crests.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to supply a brilliant shard and three crests.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Aurel's materials.",["sourceHash"]="b255bd139661f3f59e7147704451c400439985bf26fbd697cce4cbd068ef7cc1",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8341]={["aftermath"]="Aurel finished the ring and described the full disguise needed to lure a lord.",["atomIDs"]={"8341:description:1-160","8341:description:163-168","8341:description:170-240","8341:description:245-332","8341:description:335-422","8341:objective:1-88"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8341:completion:1-7","8341:completion:9-64","8341:completion:69-80","8341:completion:82-98","8341:completion:103-242","8341:completion:244-313","8341:completion:315-360"},["opening"]="Greater stones were reserved for the cult's highest servants. Aurel proposed adding a ring of lordship to the existing disguise, using brilliant shards and signets from the council.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring five shards and three signets.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied the ring materials.",["sourceHash"]="ff3c1ec11c65c5cf6f647a539ea3b25aca3fb1d8dd68ea063d7e59ab90d51c16",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8343]={["aftermath"]="Aurel confirmed her belief that she knew how to summon a lord and prepared to explain.",["atomIDs"]={"8343:description:1-104","8343:description:107-199","8343:description:202-243","8343:description:248-275","8343:description:278-313","8343:objective:1-43"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8343:completion:1-23","8343:completion:25-85","8343:completion:87-118"},["opening"]="Aurel believed a ruling council member could now be summoned. Huum referred the next discussion to her because the proposed discovery carried both promise and danger.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to hear Aurel's new method.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} consulted her at the Hold.",["sourceHash"]="d1ea511a7c9c52f84765946a550e0527190d4cc1d6bf15cba0c832fced23d663",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8348]={["atomIDs"]={"8348:description:1-65","8348:description:68-98","8348:description:103-155","8348:description:158-201","8348:description:204-276","8348:description:279-321","8348:objective:1-58"},["opening"]="Bor welcomed the discovery of how to reach a duke, then demanded evidence of defeating one. He expected a signet to demonstrate that the council's servants could be struck rather than merely contacted.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover an abyssal signet.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the signet to Bor.",["sourceHash"]="cbd283b3df11dcb71cfd86675112631777e98b9e727f2eeb384ffb3dabe6b7f5",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8349]={["atomIDs"]={"8349:description:1-86","8349:description:89-142","8349:description:147-160","8349:description:163-213","8349:objective:1-41"},["opening"]="Aurel's medallion made a new kind of encounter possible. Bor would decide the next task against the council now that its duke could be summoned.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to consult Bor with the prepared disguise.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Bor at the Hold.",["sourceHash"]="7bea99274d0341b74b0daeb5d6e9718e077f3b97f4dd890ce68a5847f100ecc2",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8351]={["atomIDs"]={"8351:description:1-133","8351:description:136-199","8351:objective:1-41"},["opening"]="The upgraded disguise could pass for the cult's ruling rank. Aurel expected Bor to have a mission suited to that dangerous access.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to hear Bor's next assignment.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Bor about the ruling council.",["sourceHash"]="28ce9dc4936e0ac94f3905243cba4f73d95403bc523ea07fbd400c359c7023f8",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8352]={["aftermath"]="Bor expressed astonishment that the lord had been defeated and offered the prepared acknowledgment.",["atomIDs"]={"8352:description:1-39","8352:description:42-122","8352:description:127-176","8352:description:179-204","8352:description:207-310","8352:description:313-373","8352:description:378-460","8352:objective:1-58"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"8352:completion:1-6","8352:completion:8-18","8352:completion:20-34","8352:completion:36-40","8352:completion:42-51","8352:completion:53-148"},["opening"]="Bor's next demand reached an abyssal lord and warned that a small group might not suffice. The requested scepter would prove the outcome without assuming any companions already stood ready.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover an abyssal scepter.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the scepter to Bor.",["sourceHash"]="d166844558092122f45feea6d3c0c9d9ee36a6feacfe7f4df7510ef731be351f",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8353]={["atomIDs"]={"8353:description:1-47","8353:description:50-125","8353:description:130-189","8353:description:191-211","8353:description:214-240","8353:description:242-279","8353:description:281-340","8353:description:345-389","8353:description:392-415","8353:objective:1-91"},["editorialVersion"]=2,["endingAtomIDs"]={"8353:completion:1-10","8353:completion:13-26","8353:completion:28-45","8353:completion:50-68"},["opening"]="Firebrew agrees to give an Ironforge Mint for the sick child's collection. Even a charitable courier must perform the holiday's trick, which he has chosen to be a chicken impression.",["pending"]="{actor} would cluck for Firebrew.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} performed Firebrew's trick and completed the mint exchange.",["sourceHash"]="26e7e9b035095a1b9cf3a35eedd014f8ec692132054b2eb84479e5ba57a66c0d",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8354]={["atomIDs"]={"8354:description:1-47","8354:description:50-125","8354:description:130-189","8354:description:191-211","8354:description:214-240","8354:description:242-279","8354:description:281-340","8354:description:345-389","8354:description:392-415","8354:objective:1-89"},["editorialVersion"]=2,["endingAtomIDs"]={"8354:completion:1-10","8354:completion:13-26","8354:completion:28-45","8354:completion:50-68"},["opening"]="Norman's Undercity Mint has an intentionally silly price. Helping a sick child does not exempt the courier from clucking like a chicken before the innkeeper.",["pending"]="{actor} would perform a chicken emote for Norman.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Norman's mint trick.",["sourceHash"]="6031e27394be2d7486277357904192600356195b6f0401ba34c0cf6a6d78c6d6",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
